  "conformsToProfile": "https://uofa.net/vocab#ProfileMinimal",
  "name": "PhysMAP applicability screen: Gnielinski closure asked about the pipe entrance region (NACA TN-1451)",
  "description": "Hand-written in the shape the surrogate pack's external-annotation rule defines, from PhysMAP's real inputs (NACA TN-1451 Fig. 10, 85 points; PhysMAP 0.2.5, commit 675729b). PhysMAP's current v0.6 export does not yet carry W-SURR pattern ids, source: external, or the structured observation fields, so this package was built by dev/tools/scripts/build_physmap_examples.py rather than exported. A pipe's Nusselt number is predicted from (Re, Pr) by the Gnielinski (1976) correlation, which is validated for fully developed flow (x/D >= 10), and is then asked about the entrance region. x/D is not a surrogate input, so the training-envelope check (W-SURR-03) and input-based OOD detectors stay silent; the closure check (W-SURR-05) fires on all 45 entrance points and stays quiet on the 40 fully developed points. The 45 annotations arrive with no Disposition: each carries a recommendedAction, which is a recommendation and not a disposition. solverTruth here is the NACA measurement, not a solver.",
  "couName": "Local Nusselt number in a heated circular pipe, entrance region included",
  "intendedUse": "Predict local Nu along the pipe from (Re, Pr) alone, as a fast stand-in for measurement or CFD.",
  "assuranceLevel": "Medium",
  "decision": "Not accepted",
  "modelRiskLevel": 2,
